# Write editing session (text shell): sh tests/shots.sh EMU SD writee 45 T1 ...
# A new document W1.MD typed with the format keys: a heading (ctrl-1), bold on a
# selection (ctrl-B), a numbered list (Enter continues it, Enter on an empty item ends
# it), italic on the word at the cursor (ctrl-I), a quote, a nested bullet (Tab), code
# (ctrl-E), undo and redo; ctrl-S saves it (it has a name). The file must equal
# tests/write-w1.md. Then File > New (ctrl-N: "Untitled.md"), the toolbar clicked with the
# mouse: Heading 1, Bold armed and "milk" typed bold, Bold again (out of it); ctrl-S: Save
# as suggests "Untitled.md", "NOTES" typed: saved as NOTES.md, which must equal
# tests/write-notes.md. Shot times (s): 18.0 34.0 39.5 41.0 43.0
#   18.0 a numbered list being typed
#   34.0 the document after it was saved
#   39.5 the new document typed with the toolbar (the pointer on Bold: its name below)
#   41.0 Save as: the name suggested
#   43.0 saved as NOTES.md (the title)
1500 {esc}
+1500 write W1.MD\n
5000 Notes{dE0}1{uE0}{end}\n\nWrite is a word processor for the Atari816.
